From da48261243caa11693a4e65fd5d958df16326f1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: silentsudin <25103587+silentsudin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:21:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] drivers: add BF63112 protocol and SPI transport

Add the dependency-free parts of a driver for the Betterlife BF63112
fingerprint module (ACPI\BF63112, Intel LPSS SPI), recovered from the
vendor Windows UMDF driver 9.39.15.26:

- bf63112_proto.[ch]: frame layout
  AA | L:u32 LE | 16 x 0 | 4C op phase 00 arg:u16 len:u32 data | pad16 | CRC-32,
  with L = 20 + align16 (10 + data_len) and CRC-32/ISO-HDLC over every
  preceding byte, including the 0xAA.  A data-less query is 41 bytes with
  L = 36.  The answer uses the same layout: opcode at offset 22, phase at
  23, body length at 27 and body at 31.

- bf63112_spi.[ch]: selector (opcode & 0x3f) << 1 for a host read and
  0x80 | ((opcode & 0x3f) << 1) for a host write, submitted as one
  two-entry SPI_IOC_MESSAGE.  Answer deadlines are 1000/5000 ms (2000/4016
  for restore), with a cancel settle and an optional reset pulse.  Only the
  read opcodes 0xA0, 0xA1, 0xB3, 0xC0, 0xC1 and the 0x2D status register
  are allowlisted, so a destructive opcode cannot be sent by accident.

- bf63112_acpi.[ch]: bounds-checked parser for the _CRS resource template
  (SpiSerialBus, GpioInt/GpioIo, small/extended IRQ), so the bus parameters
  come from firmware instead of being hard-coded.

- bf63112_discover.[ch]: locates the spidev node whose modalias is
  acpi:BF63112.

These files use only <stdint.h>/<stddef.h> and libc, with no GLib and no
libfprint header, so the userspace bring-up tools and their tests can share
the same code.

Remaining unknowns: nothing here has run against the sensor.  The answer
framing is assumed to be byte-for-byte the request layout.  The SPI clock,
mode, word size and GPIO polarity are only known from _CRS and have not been
read on hardware.  Whether the module echoes the request phase is
unverified.  The SM2/SM3/SM4 session handshake (0xA2) is not implemented
because the read-only queries do not need it.

The licence line is a TODO in each file: the project owner has not chosen a
licence for this subtree yet.  It must be set (LGPL-2.1-or-later, to match
libfprint) before this series is submitted.

Provenance: facts recovered by observation of the vendor Windows UMDF
driver; no vendor code, strings or binary content was copied.
